---
// nerdr on a laptop with two servers: a client of each machine's core,
// the servers' over SSH through nerdr bridge. See use/remote.mdx.
---
<figure class="nerdr-diagram">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 760 360" role="img" aria-labelledby="dm-title dm-desc">
		<title id="dm-title">nerdr on a laptop with two servers</title>
		<desc id="dm-desc">
			nerdr on the laptop connects to the laptop's own core, and over SSH
			to nerdr bridge on each server, which connects to that server's core.
			Each core runs its machine's agents, worktrees and git.
		</desc>
		<defs>
			<marker id="dm-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
				<path class="arrowhead" d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" />
			</marker>
			<marker id="dm-arrow-accent" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
				<path class="arrowhead accent" d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" />
			</marker>
		</defs>

		<!-- The laptop -->
		<rect class="region" x="10" y="10" width="250" height="340" rx="10" />
		<text class="region-label" x="28" y="36">Your laptop</text>

		<rect class="box accent" x="30" y="56" width="210" height="64" rx="7" />
		<text class="title mono" x="135" y="83" text-anchor="middle">nerdr</text>
		<text class="sub" x="135" y="104" text-anchor="middle">what you see and click</text>

		<rect class="box" x="30" y="168" width="210" height="64" rx="7" />
		<text class="title" x="135" y="195" text-anchor="middle">core</text>
		<text class="sub" x="135" y="216" text-anchor="middle">this machine's tabs</text>

		<rect class="box" x="30" y="276" width="210" height="52" rx="7" />
		<text class="sub" x="135" y="307" text-anchor="middle">agents · worktrees · git</text>

		<path class="edge" d="M135 120 V166" marker-end="url(#dm-arrow)" />
		<path class="edge" d="M135 232 V274" marker-end="url(#dm-arrow)" />

		<!-- Server box -->
		<rect class="region" x="480" y="10" width="270" height="160" rx="10" />
		<text class="region-label host mono" x="498" y="36">box</text>
		<rect class="box" x="496" y="50" width="112" height="54" rx="7" />
		<text class="title mono" x="552" y="73" text-anchor="middle">nerdr bridge</text>
		<text class="sub mono" x="552" y="93" text-anchor="middle">~/src</text>
		<rect class="box" x="626" y="50" width="108" height="54" rx="7" />
		<text class="title" x="680" y="74" text-anchor="middle">core</text>
		<text class="sub" x="680" y="93" text-anchor="middle">box's tabs</text>
		<rect class="box" x="496" y="120" width="238" height="36" rx="7" />
		<text class="sub" x="615" y="143" text-anchor="middle">agents · worktrees · git</text>
		<path class="edge" d="M608 77 H624" marker-end="url(#dm-arrow)" />
		<path class="edge" d="M680 104 V118" marker-end="url(#dm-arrow)" />

		<!-- Server gpu -->
		<rect class="region" x="480" y="190" width="270" height="160" rx="10" />
		<text class="region-label host mono" x="498" y="216">gpu</text>
		<rect class="box" x="496" y="230" width="112" height="54" rx="7" />
		<text class="title mono" x="552" y="253" text-anchor="middle">nerdr bridge</text>
		<text class="sub mono" x="552" y="273" text-anchor="middle">~</text>
		<rect class="box" x="626" y="230" width="108" height="54" rx="7" />
		<text class="title" x="680" y="254" text-anchor="middle">core</text>
		<text class="sub" x="680" y="273" text-anchor="middle">gpu's tabs</text>
		<rect class="box" x="496" y="300" width="238" height="36" rx="7" />
		<text class="sub" x="615" y="323" text-anchor="middle">agents · worktrees · git</text>
		<path class="edge" d="M608 257 H624" marker-end="url(#dm-arrow)" />
		<path class="edge" d="M680 284 V298" marker-end="url(#dm-arrow)" />

		<!-- SSH from the laptop's nerdr to each bridge -->
		<path class="edge accent" d="M240 82 C 360 82, 380 77, 494 77" marker-end="url(#dm-arrow-accent)" />
		<text class="edge-label accent mono" x="368" y="70" text-anchor="middle">ssh box</text>
		<path class="edge accent" d="M240 96 C 380 96, 370 257, 494 257" marker-end="url(#dm-arrow-accent)" />
		<text class="edge-label accent mono" x="352" y="206" text-anchor="end">ssh gpu</text>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>
		nerdr on your laptop is a client of each machine's core: its own, and
		one on each server, reached over SSH. The cores do not know about each
		other, and the agents work on where they are when you close nerdr.
	</figcaption>
</figure>
